# Product evals stay current

Kampaku’s evaluation bar lives in `docs/eval/` (suite protocols `00`–`20`). Run board and learnings live under `docs/eval/results/`. Automated locks live in `apps/core/tests/eval/` and `apps/web/e2e/eval-*.spec.ts`.

## New behavior must land in evals

When you add or change emperor-visible product behavior (tools, staffing, plan/execute, wiki, HITL, isolation, UI gates, stranger repos):

1. **Prefer an existing suite** whose promise already covers the gap — extend its oracle, Automated tests table, and cited unit/e2e.
2. **Add a new suite** only when no later file owns the promise (follow `docs/eval/results/LEARNINGS.md` disposition style; update `docs/eval/README.md` suite order).
3. Lock the promise with **automated tests** (U4). Scenario copy stays in stubs/prompts/args — not baked into product-tool defaults (**BOARD E-010** pattern).
4. Score and evidence stay in the suite markdown; open product gaps on `docs/eval/results/BOARD.md` in product language.

## Re-run when changes can affect evals

Before calling work done, if the diff can change suite outcomes (runtime tools/session stubs, PM/wiki/questions, worker execution, web surfaces cited by eval e2e, skills/prompts that steer emperor tools):

1. Re-run the **affected** `apps/core/tests/eval/eval-*.test.ts` / `apps/web/e2e/eval-*.spec.ts` (and LLM smoke when the suite claims it).
2. For renames or shared-path changes, re-run **01…N** automated tests that cite those surfaces (see `docs/eval/00-protocol.md` incremental-fixes rule).
3. Do not leave a suite marked green from an old SHA if its locked promise or cited tests changed — fresh evidence or re-score.
4. Do not delete or soften an eval assertion only to make a product change pass; update the suite oracle when the intended product promise itself changed.

## Quick map

| Change area | Typical suites / tests |
|-------------|------------------------|
| Inventory / project metadata | 01–02 |
| Staffing / roster / domain-agnostic | 03, 18 |
| Intent clarify / scope | 05, 12 |
| Stranger bootstrap / plan / execute / wiki / done | 06–11 |
| HITL / operator UI | 10, 16 |
| Interrupt / least privilege / host isolation | 13–15 |
| Provider fidelity | 17 |
| Integration arc | 19 |
